- Handle mix of crop and non-crop
   plots

For the Ag plots in the mix:
- Option 1: Assign "peak" on per 
   plot basis (peak mass across all plots
   may be a mix of harvest dates).
- Option 2: Choose crop/bout with 
   greatest mass as "peak". Not all plots
   may be planted with this crop.
   --&gt; unclear how to implement b/c
          not all plots sampled every "bout"
- Option 3 (yes): Option 1 but pull
   plots from crop sites out into separate table.

For non-Ag plots in the mix:
- Option 1: Latest bout in year
- Option 2 (yes): Identify peak biomass
   on per plot basis.

Plots with tTP = "No" --&gt; 0 biomass<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
